  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-27378529" secondary-reporter="0" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Netherlands Enterprise Agency</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Myanmar&apos;s seed sector enabling environment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop an internationally competitive, vibrant seed sector supported by a conducive enabling environment, with the competencies on the ground to implement regulations and support companies. The goal is to establish a foundation for high-quality seed production, catering to domestic and international markets. In the objective, two &#x2018;enablers&#x2019; stand out:&#x2022;	A conducive enabling environment, including a well-functioning Plant Variety Protection (PVP) system and improving the Quality Assurance (QA) system and the practical seed chain coordination. &#x2022;	Competence to implement regulations and support seed producers. These competencies include the capacity to implement regulations and the technical knowledge and skills to produce quality seed in a business-oriented way.It entails supporting the transformation of a public-dominated intermediate seed system to a more private and market-oriented one. These competencies will be developed through on-the-job training, technical advice and coaching.</narrative>
  </description>
